# This frozen package ships NO restricted / person-level data.
# The person-level files are already excluded at build time (the assembler drops any
# CSV whose header carries a person-id column). These patterns are a SECOND safety net
# so that a local re-run of the pipeline cannot accidentally commit identifiable data.
#
# Parent cohorts (CHARLS, KLoSA, MHAS, RAND HRS) are access-restricted and NOT
# redistributable; see README.md "Reproducing from source data".

# --- raw cohort downloads (person-level, ~8 GB) ---
data/raw/

# --- person-level working files regenerated by an analysis run ---
data/processed/intl/incident/personperiod_*
data/processed/intl/incident/*personperiod*
data/processed/intl/incident/hrs_times*
results/**/*personperiod_pooled*
results/**/*leakage_audit*.csv
analysis/output/**/*personperiod*

# --- build / scratch artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: the aggregate model outputs under data/processed/intl/incident/incident_*.csv and
# everything under results/tables|reports|deliverables are INTENTIONALLY tracked — they are
# de-identified aggregate numbers and the figures, and the audit gates read them.
